    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0581" n="1315" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1315"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram<anchor n="1" xml:id="d582-f1"/> received last night regarding Lenz
                    and missionary protection indicates a better spirit on the part of the Turkish
                    Government than your preceding telegram showed, and suggests that good
                    management may avert proposed formal demand for passports. Firmly impress upon
                    Turkish Government our right to be promptly answered as to just demands, and our
                    confidence that the answers will be satisfactory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
